- How would you test for liveness under shutdowns and timeouts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of crash‑consistency in non‑volatile memory, proper cache‑line flush semantics, and cross‑socket ordering. It probes how to design durable queues and recoveries with minimal latency impact.

## Key Concepts
- PMEM durability and flush/fence ordering (clwb/clflushopt, sfence)
- Release/acquire memory ordering and per‑slot sequencing
- Crash recovery and replay correctness in a bounded buffer

## Code Example
